{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1205820-durance-ideas","id":1205820,"title":"Durance Ideas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-11T16:40:26-07:00","id":1205820,"title":"Durance Ideas?","content":"Simply put, this thread is for us to post ideas we might have for durances. Whether they be glossed over backstories, or actual prequel stories. Let's see what fun ideas others have come up with!<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Climbing the Food Chain:</b> Even by Changeling standards, this particular durance is considered to be ruthlessly merciless. It seems that one of the True Fae was disappointed with the mortal version of the Hunger Games and decided to create their own variation for entertainment purposes. A popular blood sport in the world of Arcadia, <i>'Climbing the Food Chain'</i> is a game that pits mortal slaves against their environment and forces them to fight for their very survival. The game lasts for one year, with most contestants dying horribly within that time span. Those who manage to survive are recognized as having become top of the food chain, and are allowed to go free. Though after spending a year in Arcadia, they do not return in the same state they left.<br /> <br /> The terms of the game are simple. At the start of each year, the contestants are deposited on a remote island and are stripped of every material possession, including their very clothing. Naked and defenseless, the contestants must hunt, forage, craft and build everything they own with their own two hands. Or they can trade resources and services with another contestant if they lack the knowledge of how to do so.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, Climbing the Food Chain has only one other rule: Survive by any means possible. The island is littered with things that are trying to kill you and there is only a finite supply of resources to go around. The game starts in the Spring and progresses through the seasons of Summer, Autumn and finally Winter. Eventually, contestants are forced to compete with each other to preserve what they have. Often, such competitions turn deadly as those involved become desperate to rid themselves of nearby rivals.<br /> <br /> <br /> After the year is over and the winners are declared, those who failed to make it to the end find themselves revived by their Fae masters to endure another year of extreme survival exercise. Unfortunately, the start of a new game means losing all the resources they accumulated in the previous one, so they have to start over from the bottom!<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Past Champions:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Amazonia</i> - Female Ogre, toughest bitch in the land.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Tyger</i> - Male Beast, his time on the island awakened his most primal instincts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Jaime Kline</i> - Female Darkling, she cruelly sacrificed her allies in order to preserve her own life.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Mason Chapman</i> - Male Wizened, his tools and structures were more advanced than the primitive creations of his fellow contestants.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Terra</i> - Female Elemental, communing with the natural forces of the island awakened shamanistic powers within her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Tyson Graham</i> - Male Fairest, under his leadership, the other contestants managed to form a tribal community, working together to increase their odds of success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-11-2018, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T16:54:04-07:00","id":1205824,"title":"","content":"I see those guys would get along well in werewolf packs and Beast broods. <br /> <br /> I once had an idea where the mandatory military service in my country was twisted into a Durance. Where the mortal service grinds upon body and soul (and leaves too many people broken for the higher-ups to be comfortable talking about) but is otherwise banal, the Arcadian version would be much more wondrous. In the sense of \u201cHey, what use is a drill if you don\u2019t actually fight with enemy troops?\u201d sense of wondrous, typical Fae style. <br /> <br /> Now, if I only had access to Changeling 2E rules... (sad)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T16:59:44-07:00","id":1205827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1205820-durance-ideas?p=1205824#post1205824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see those guys would get along well in werewolf packs and Beast broods.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funny you should say that. The idea is a remodeled interpretation of a furry themed survival RP I tried to run in the past. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> And yes, I feel for you. I wish 2E would get here already. I've decided it's going to be the next Chronicles of Darkness book I get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T17:33:17-07:00","id":1205833,"title":"","content":"I had an old character who was the nurse to a genuinely horrifying medical-themed Fae who was all about magical surgery and sticking things together that shouldn\u2019t be. She helped painfully make a few other changelings, and carried a lot of guilt over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:01:50-07:00","id":1205880,"title":"","content":"I believe Atamajakki might remember it, but a character I had planned out but never played much with had an interesting progression of different durance ideas.<br /> <br /> Idea first started out with him getting caught by his Keeper when he signed up for what the Keeper advertised as a home for young adults aging out of the foster care system and worried about becoming homeless. The Keeper acted like they (I imagined them as manifesting as the faculty and staff instead of a single authority figure) had a sort of True Fae's Burden complex and brought in uncivilized mortal &quot;children&quot; to teach them the alien manners of the Fae. To quote myself: &quot;So they're running a sort of Victorian Domby Hall/Work House Domain, but without any regard for Euclidean geometry or the laws of time and it's trying to teach you that you should be ashamed of thinking that gravity pulls you down instead of pushing you purple or just doing whatever the hell I want it to do.&quot; While you are there, you regress in age until you are as young, weak and plastic-minded as the staff thinks you are.<br /> <br /> Later on, I decided I wanted him to be a ratman, so I added a second, rival keeper called the Rat King. He and The Academy were locked in a wyrd-blessed contest to see which side of the fae was better: the chaos of wild, nature spirit faeries (think stuff like Maenads and Satyrs) or the byzantine, backstabbing courts of the gentry. The Rat King's role was to corrupt and undermine the Academy's lessons, and thus was barred from obtaining his own Changelings from Ironside, instead having to entice over and sneak off with the Academy's wards through promises of debauchery, freedom and vengeance. His gang is sort of a dark Lost Boys, but filthier in all senses of the word. They live in the basements, pipes and the walls of the Academy, living through cycles of feast and famine depending on what or who they stole today.<br /> <br /> Then my ST didn't like that and he got transported to a realm with three Fae playing out a battle between &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot;, with a neutral tavern where the last of the three gave just enough respite to the weary to keep them fighting on. Honestly, not as fond of this one for my own reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:18:39-07:00","id":1205886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1205820-durance-ideas?p=1205880#post1205880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then my ST didn't like that and he got transported to a realm with three Fae playing out a battle between &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Welp... speaking of that!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is another idea that was remodeled from a previous RP of mine. It's original name was Monsters and Fairy Folk, but obviously that name would be confusing in the Changeling setting.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>King and Queen:</b> Another popular blood sport created by the same Fae responsible for <i>Climbing the Food Chain</i>. King and Queen is an elaborate war game pitting two factions against each other for control of the realm. The first faction is lead by the Bright Queen, who's influence turns the realm vibrant and beautiful. The second faction is lead by the Dark King, who's influence turns the realm corrupted and hideous. The state of the realm is constantly in flux, changing its layout and appearance as the two factions claim and lose territory over the course of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ending the game is simple in theory, all you have to do is slay the enemy faction's ruler. Of course, being part of the True Fae, they don't actually die, but that's beside the point. In any case, once the king or queen is defeated, the realm falls under the control of the winning faction until such time as they decide to play again. Then the realm is reset and the war begins anew. Because the game persists until one leader is eliminated, the length of this durance can vary drastically between each time it is experienced. With campaigns lasting anywhere from several months to several decades.<br /> <br /> As a way to make the war even more exciting, or maybe just to drag it out as long as possible, those who fall to the enemy are later revived as new recruits in their rival's army. Thus the King and Queen are constantly replenishing their lost troops by stealing from their enemy!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Changelings created by this durance are labeled as deserters by their supportive factions. They abandoned the war in order to flee across the border (i.e, the Hedge) to foreign lands (i.e, Earth). Desertion is not tolerated by either side of the war, and both the King and Queen have dispatched agents to hunt down the traitors and drag them back to face their proper punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-11-2018, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T23:35:40-07:00","id":1205951,"title":"","content":"I have a number of Durances, all hypothetical and all ones I will probably never get to play. Still, I'll list them for funsies.<br /> <br /> <b>The City That Knows Crime</b><br /> <br /> The City is a Fae who targets wrong-doers, law breakers and criminals of all forms and sizes. It doesn't matter if they're actually <i>guilty</i> of the purported crimes - it will take a school kid whose locker had a gun planted in it as soon as it would target a drug dealer or a serial stabber. The percieved crime is as important as the genuine crime, and it will drag those who catch its interest in with its chains. Once it has them, it will pull them into an asylum, force them to recant their crimes until they can provide no break or comfort, and then offers them the chance to become &quot;better&quot;. Masks, suits of animal hides, weapons, cloaks of shadow and so much more; the lining of the articles is the contract with the Keeper, and once donned to suit the new indentity it is fused into their flesh. They are then released onto the City, to partake in crimes as gangs, to steal and invade the homes of &quot;civilians&quot; and do as they once did with their powers while evading the &quot;police&quot; that roam the streets. Any crimes committed without being caught are not crimes, but being caught or being stolen from by another gang means they have committed one and are to face the asylum for punishment. After all, it is the city itself; it knows what is done, and the civilians and cops that inhabit it are the discarded faces of its inmates. Leaving is a crime...but after a while, guilt or the pleasure of doing as they once did and being effectively rewarded for it keeps the Changelings in. It is both stick and carrot.<br /> <br /> Basically, it's if Gotham City itself created the supervillains that roam its streets. Simply put, it's not a nice place.<br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <br /> <b>The Midnight Bus</b><br /> <br /> The Midtnight Bus is a triple decker bus, and it rules the streets of its domain. It targets people who are stuck in the backroads, who speed (and crash) in the dark or even just approaches people who wait in the dead of night waiting for the last bus home. Once it has its target wrapped up in red carpet, it scurries them away through the Hedge at a breakneck pace, into its realm and then taken for &quot;processing&quot;. Its realm is one massive motorway, with streets looping around themselves, garages and bridges that span over other bridges. Only vehicles may roam the roads - Ogres and Darklings are most common, though any Kith may be vehicles by way of &quot;Props and Scenary&quot;, though Elementals are more commonly the streetsigns and lamps on the sides of the roads. Of course, they must be very careful where they stay the night; The Midnight Bus also has established police cruises that take errant vehicles to established &quot;Chop Shops&quot;, which are basically processing and punishment for rule breakers. Woe be a Changeling who stops in a garage and finds it's a Chop Shop by accident, where the Wizened are eager to practice their speed in dissasembly...<br /> <br /> Changelings who escape better resemble Transformers than anything else, usually covered in chrome, metalic paint and rubber at their fingertips, their bodies shapeshifting for their fae magic. Mechanics from the realm are...not looked kindly upon. Sure, some were eager to keep the vehicles running sharp, but this usually came out as surgery for the poor vehicles, and anastetic is not for cars or mopeds...<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>The Wordsmith</b><br /> <br /> Imagine the world as a blank canvas, literally white and fiberous, waiting for ink, paint and effort to be given definition. That is the realm the Wordsmith is, and it is the medium for his greatest masterpiece, whatever that may be each day. He is the ultimate writer, the greatest of tale tellers, and his words literally fly off the page for the reader to experience. The problem is that he needs inspiration, raw creation to get his works going - that much genius doesn't leave room for imagination after all. That's what his Changelings are for. All of them are either workforce or the engines of creativity, either brewing the ink and material the Wordsmith needs or drawing and living within the environments befitting their roles. Artist Beasts may craft a cave and their food over and over again, whereas the Fairest would have to draw their poster bed as well as the edible flowers they arrange at their bedside table; meanwhile, the Leechfingers draw out the blood from their victims to be replaced with ink, until the victim's body has a particular color running through it, and the Chatellaine are left to make the physical alterations. Anything drawn is torn down if not perfect, whether the Changeling is inside their creation or not, and anything perfect is taken and put into a new story and given context within it.<br /> <br /> Without ink, a Changeling can run for hours and be caught by someone at a brisk walking pace in five minutes, and one can dig a tunnel for hours only to pop their head up where they started - space has no meaning without signposts. It makes escape hard without leaving behind the signs of how you did it. Of course, who has time to escape when you need to draw your environment with perfect precision and your fingers are the pens, or to kep the rivers of ink and pools of pulp clear of any impurities. The Wordsmith would be ever so cross if he found anything out of place, before or during his masterpiece's creation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T04:50:19-07:00","id":1208394,"title":"","content":"<b>The Chamber of Screams: </b>A most nerve wracking realm, the so called 'Chamber of Screams' appears to be a vast, empty room comprised of androgynous faces. The walls, floors and ceiling are all human faces with no distinguishing features that make them stand out from each other. As if that wasn't disturbing enough, every one of the faces is in a perpetual state of either terror or pain, causing them to scream at the top of their lungs and filling the chamber with a cacophony of noise.<br /> <br /> Spending any degree of time in this chamber would be uncomfortable, but the worst thing you can possibly do here is lose your composure. Because once you join in the screaming, that's when the room begins to shift, absorbing you into its structure. If that happens, you'll become just another face in the Chamber of Screams.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fortunately, this does not have to be the ultimate fate of those who find themselves trapped within. Once in a while, one of the faces summons up the strength of will to free themselves. Somehow, they manage to give themselves enough wiggle room to get an arm or a leg free, and then keep it up until they've pried themselves loose, once separated from the rest of the architecture, they can set to work on finding a way out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T08:39:01-07:00","id":1208462,"title":"","content":"<b>Cogs in the Machine:</b> the True Fae is building something, or maybe it <i>is </i>something, an infinitely intricate mechanical monstrosity with endless inputs but no discernable outputs. It's not the God-Machine: the mechanisms are circular and ultimately self-defeating (think &quot;robot that switches itself off&quot; on a vast scale) and it exists more for the sake of its rickety architecture than to actually do anything. It mostly creates Wizened to do the work of building and maintaining the illogical morass of the machine, or Elementals--brass and steel serve as parts, while fire, steam and electricity keep the whole thing (nominally) powered.<br /> <br /> Malfunctions are the most common opportunity Changelings have to escape the Machine, though some have been known to indulge in deliberate sabotage. It's always risky, though, as any &quot;broken&quot; parts (including the technicians) are likely to get violently &quot;recycled&quot; if they can be singled out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T10:12:49-07:00","id":1208484,"title":"","content":"I once had a Changeling whose Durance was basically the ME!ME!ME! music video. I'd link but it's pretty heavily NSFW. General idea was the Keeper was his Keeper had recently finished reshaping their Titles and decided to play a sort of Erinyes for jilted and emotionally abused lovers. <br /> <br /> The character came out as a fairly standard Wizened though, with his only real defining feature being his eyestalks. Kinda boring compared to his durance.<br /> <br /> Looking back, if I ever went back to that character, I'd make the connection to ME!ME!ME! less direct. Instead of it being how he remembered his Durance in its entirety, the video would just seem disturbingly familiar to him in ways he couldn't place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}